ds:concept.Design-tokens-Color---reference a ds:Concept;
    ds:name "Design tokens: Color - reference";
    ds:summary "This document lists all tokens that are needed in relation to color. For the most part these tokens will be of the “color” type. But some tokens like the lightness adjustment tokens for interactive states might fall under different categories.\n\nThe token tables in this specification are a snapshot of the tokens that we have decided on at the time of writing this specification. They are static so people in the future can reference the state of the token at the time of writing this specification. For an overview of all tokens that have been worked on you can reference the following documents:\n\n- [Resolvers](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/u/0/d/1OSa9BECoky3BFb-gaQfnbLbVfzfMp_r-Ot7ChcxDFTE/edit)\n- [Global design tokens](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XXBNXVasSr1yfk_w-7Wpaeoag3tQM0y4YK6P_RYWFmU/edit?gid=561378064#gid=561378064)\n- [Apps design tokens](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hTG_MXOEYpb6U3SVpCFNnQSDzB_LrsrABwsK3tZosH4/edit?gid=0#gid=0)\n- [Docs design tokens](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Hk4PHbug3v8kNe65Qg0O0WMqGDI8Uhf1vvyLnD5Rv0U/edit?gid=0#gid=0)\n- [Sites design tokens](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/179tDsNJYGKlJJbn7gxJ4khqZ6nPubaJkHZyRgH-vUGk/edit?gid=0#gid=0)";
    ds:tier ds:global;
    ds:content "## Tokens\n\nThe code with which these tokens have been generated can be found under the [code tab](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vL0W-MA5QOLnQ_yZMt1xJ-tsVmiy5UD8613XCnpdi0w/edit?tab=t.8tobzs2rlba5).\n\n### **Primitive tokens**\n\n#### Black\n\nPrimitive Tokens\n\n\n\nTable 90\n\n​\n\n#### White\n\nTable 91\n\n​\n\n#### Gray\n\nTable 92\n\n​\n\n#### Orange\n\nTable 93\n\n​\n\n#### Teal\n\nTable 94\n\n​\n\n#### Blue\n\nTable 95\n\n​\n\n#### Purple\n\nTable 96\n\n​\n\n#### Green\n\nTable 97\n\n​\n\n#### Red\n\nTable 98\n\n​\n\n#### Yellow\n\nTable 99\n\n​\n\n#### Aubergine\n\nTable 100\n\n​\n\n#### Numbers\n\n#### Hue\n\nTable 101\n\n#### Chroma\n\nTable 102\n\n​\n\n#### Opacity\n\nTable 103\n\n​\n\n#### Lightness border\n\nTable 104\n\n​\n\n#### Lightness foreground ghost\n\nTable 105\n\n​  \n\n\n#### Lightness foreground input\n\nTable 106\n\n​\n\n#### Lightness foreground primary\n\nTable 107\n\n​\n\n#### Lightness foreground secondary\n\nTable 108\n\n​\n\n#### Lightness foreground navigation\n\nTable 109\n\n​\n\n#### Lightness text\n\nTable 110\n\n​\n\n### **Semantic tokens**\n\n#### Light mode\n\n**Backdrop**\n\nTable 111\n\n​\n\n**Background**\n\nTable 112\n\n​\n\n**Border**\n\nTable 113\n\n​\n\n**Brand**\n\nTable 114\n\n​\n\n**Focus Ring**\n\nTable 115\n\n​\n\n**Foreground ghost**\n\nTable 116\n\n​\n\n**Foreground navigation**\n\nTable 117\n\n​\n\n**Foreground input**\n\nTable 118\n\n​\n\n**Foreground primary**\n\nTable 119\n\n​\n\n**Foreground secondary**\n\nTable 120\n\n​\n\n**Foreground controls**\n\nTable 121\n\n​\n\n**Icon**\n\nTable 122\n\n​\n\n**Text**\n\nTable 123\n\n​\n\n#### Dark mode\n\n**Backdrop**\n\nTable 124\n\n​\n\n**Background**\n\nTable 125\n\n​\n\n**Border**\n\nTable 126\n\n​\n\n**Brand**\n\nTable 127\n\n​\n\n**Focus Ring**\n\nTable 128\n\n​\n\n**Foreground ghost**\n\nTable 129\n\n​\n\n**Foreground navigation**\n\nTable 130\n\n​\n\n**Foreground input**\n\nTable 131\n\n​\n\n**Foreground primary**\n\nTable 132\n\n​\n\n**Foreground secondary**\n\nTable 133\n\n​\n\n**Foreground controls**\n\nTable 134\n\n​\n\n**Icon**\n\nTable 135\n\n​\n\n**Text**\n\nTable 136\n\n​  \n";
    ds:knownEdgeCases "";
    ds:conceptType ds:concepttype.Reference.
